jcopelan@nyx10.cs.du.edu (Jim Copeland) writes:

>Who else out there also enjoys having a couple of strong-arm buddies along
>to soften up those big nasties?  I take great delight in trying to get a
>nice little army to go along with me on my escapades.  Any other tales
>involving fun with pets?  What are some of your favorite/unique
>combinations of/strangest pets? 

Chameleons.  It is usually a brief aquaintence (to fools turn into kamikaze
creatures like freezing spheres or yellow lights!), but you get to sample
a great range of pets.  They're easy to get too... just throw it a tripe
ration when it turns into a dog or cat, and avoid them otherwise - get ready
with teleport, in case they turn into something too powerful, and stay off the
diagonal incase they polymorph into a creature with a breath weapon.

A magic whistle helps to keep them alive - blow it when they are about to
blow it.

The best thing about them is that they are easy to kill-off or re-tame if
you lose control of them... unlike pet dragons.


ObWish:  pets should be more loyal the longer you have them for.

